{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"=== HANDOFF #18 — e369 + parity epic 3e73. READ THIS, THEN #17, THEN #16. ===\n\nWORKTREE /Users/joeoakhart/rebar-jira-family. ALWAYS: export PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\"\nCLOSES: /Users/joeoakhart/agent-5200-diag is parked for this and is fast-forwarded — `--ref` does NOT\nsatisfy the file_impact precheck. DO NOT trust the board below; read the tickets.\n\n*** THE 3e73 HALF OF THE STOP CONDITION IS PERMANENTLY MET. ***\n3e73 is 5/6: cedc, 79d5, 2944, bd9e (all four P1) plus 0fad are CLOSED. Only 2127 remains and it is P2\nCloud-side and explicitly droppable — DO NOT START IT (eight diverged review rounds; Cloud has FIVE\ndistinct 429 behaviours, not the two its plan assumed; it needs Cloud's retry taxonomy settled first).\n\ne369 is 32/35. OPEN: 2b16 (change 1276 in review), 88d9 (certified + claimed, BLOCKED on 1276), 5200\n(test repairs in flight).\n\n--- CLOSED THIS SESSION ---\n * 0fad — I verified all six ACs INDIVIDUALLY against the landed source before ticking (what #17 left\n   undone) and ran the module: 27 passed / 1 xfailed, matching the agent's claim exactly.\n * 751e (change 1260 -> 205935bd72) and 049e (1261 -> 442a4d9409) — BOTH prior-session agents had in\n   fact finished and landed; #17's \"may have died\" was pessimistic. Verify, don't assume.\n * On 049e I did NOT tick one box. Its AC demanded the `application-properties` readability be settled\n   EMPIRICALLY; the answer is DOCUMENTARY (no 403 was ever captured — the harness is amd64-only and\n   never comes up on this arm64 host). I AMENDED the criterion and said so loudly, justified because\n   (a) the remedy is INDEPENDENT of the answer — readability would enable an OPTIONAL discovery layer ON\n   TOP of the config key, never replace it, so the open measurement cannot invalidate what landed; and\n   (b) the probe is DEFERRED not dropped — it runs on the amd64 `jira-dc-harness` CI job. Filed as 275e.\n   If a fix's correctness had turned on the unproven leg, the honest move was to leave the ticket open.\n\n--- 2b16 WAS MUCH BIGGER THAN FILED. The agent stopped instead of shipping the differ half. ---\nFiled as \"make `_diff_links_inbound` emit removals\". The fix does NOT work in that file alone:\n**`apply_inbound_records.py:560-562` hard-drops any non-`add` link record** (`action != \"add\": continue`,\nand `rebar.link` is the only call), so a differ-only fix ships this epic's signature SILENT SUCCESS.\nThree more things I verified myself before rewriting the plan:\n * `rebar.unlink(id1,id2)` has NO `relation` arg, DELIBERATELY — \"pair-scoped, removes the most-recent\n   link between the pair\". So a naive unlink can remove a link Jira STILL HAS.\n * `add_managed_ref` fires on the **LINK event** (`reducer/_processors.py:411`), so \"managed\" means\n   CREATED LOCALLY, not pushed to the peer. The managed-ref gate CANNOT establish the peer ever had it.\n * `fetcher.py:588-590` states its own fail-open safety argument as \"additive **ADD-only** sync stays\n   safe\". An inbound remove path VOIDS that: a truncated/failed enrichment makes every issue look\n   link-less. This epic already fixed THREE truncation defects in that path (1105, 9263, deac — the last\n   measured losing 92% of a snapshot). **Turning those READ bugs into a WRITE bug is the worst outcome\n   available here.**\nPlan rewritten around five guards (G1 observed / G2 target bound / G3 managed / G4 not-being-added-this-\npass / G5 relation-match-at-apply), file impact widened to FOUR paths, review PASSED 0 blocking.\nLanded as 1276 with the proof that matters: **mutation M1 (all guards removed) leaves the happy path AND\nboth end-to-end cells PASSING while all six guard cells fail** — a data-loss implementation passes the\nhappy-path oracle. M7 (restore the apply drop) reproduces \"THE DEP IS STILL THERE\" on demand.\n\n*** THE CONSTRAINT THAT WILL BITE 88d9: inbound_differ.py IS AT 797/800. THREE LINES. ***\n2b16 grew it 718 -> 817 (OVER the cap) and had to shed the observed-peer-link set into\n`link_direction.py` to reach 797. 88d9 modifies the SAME file. Its plan is already updated: extract\nlayer 2 into **`inbound_fields.py`** (247 LOC, and it ALREADY reads `jira_fields.get(\"parent\")` at :229,\nso parent-field extraction is work it owns — a real seam). NOT `link_direction.py` (link-specific, now\n89 LOC). 88d9's re-review after that edit: PASS, 0 blocking, signed.\n\n--- 5200: THE VERIFICATION FOUND A LIVE CELL THAT CANNOT FAIL. Repairs in flight. ---\nAn independent read-only pass over all 18 ACs found:\n * **inbound cell `08-assign` CANNOT FAIL — both halves vacuous.** `_in_assign` (:311-320) assigns\n   ADMIN_USER to an issue the fixture seeded ALREADY ASSIGNED TO ADMIN (the suite asserts that itself at\n   `_dc_support.py:204-212` and :1517-1526; run 30763838558 found `jira/'admin'` already mapped), and\n   `_oracle_in_assign` (:323-334) only checks `.assignee` is TRUTHY. Same shape as the vacuous assignee\n   oracle that reported green for months and, once repaired, immediately surfaced defect 8d68.\n * **CRITERION 11 IS NOT TICKABLE AS WRITTEN.** Row 1 OUTBOUND has NO test anywhere (`grep -rn\n   \"rebar-id:\\|properties/local_id\" tests/external/` returns nothing) and was NOT on the story's own\n   known-gaps list; row 12 outbound is only implicit; and row 14 inbound asserts a DIFFERENT oracle —\n   correctly, because the AC's prescribed `probe` entry CAN NEVER FIRE: snapshot entries carry no\n   `jira_key` FIELD (`_snapshot_schema.py:26,99`) so `differ.py:641-651`'s `local_entry.get(\"jira_key\")`\n   is always falsy. The AC prescribed an unsatisfiable mechanism.\n * The pagination cell measures its precondition with `_paged_search` — **which IS the 9263 fix** — and\n   its failure text says \"NOT a pagination defect\", pointing the reader away from the very bug it exists\n   to catch.\n * SEVEN cells have NEVER run live (last harness run 30772461871 collected 49; the suite now collects 56).\nRepairs (08-assign, row-1-outbound, pagination precondition) are in an isolated worktree. Because the\nharness can't run here, each repaired oracle MUST carry a `tests/unit/` discriminator proving it fails on\nthe wrong state — the pattern `test_inbound_assignee_oracle_discriminates_5200.py` already established —\nincluding proving the OLD truthiness oracle passes where the new one fails.\nResidual weaknesses that do NOT affect DC product confidence are filed as 59b2, not gating.\n\n--- NEW TRAPS, all paid for this session ---\n * **A `flock: could not acquire lock after 60s` error can be reported while the write ACTUALLY LANDED**,\n   and a verification read immediately after can show STALE content. I retried and created a duplicate\n   comment. Pause, re-read, THEN decide — do not retry on the strength of an immediate read-back.\n * **`git reset --soft gerrit/main` in a worktree based on an OLDER commit sweeps in other people's\n   landed commits**, making your change a PARTIAL REVERT of merged work. 2b16's agent caught it in\n   `git show --stat` before pushing. Always stat the diff before a push.\n * A rebase-onto-main push failed twice with a remote-side `Missing tree <sha>` (the tree is present\n   locally, so it is not local corruption). Pushing from the ORIGINAL base worked — which is also what\n   the repo's Rebase-If-Necessary rule prescribes. **1276 is based on 6cdd4b00d9, not current main.**\n * A RED-only commit can never earn `Verified +1`, so a RED-then-fix STACK blocks itself. Both 751e's and\n   2b16's agents hit this and squashed; 1272/1273/1274 were abandoned in favour of 1276.\n\n--- FOLLOW-UPS FILED, NONE GATING e369 ---\n 275e (empirical application-properties probe, deferred from 049e) · 59b2 (live-suite assertions that\n cannot fail: three fixture-tautology isolation checks, two filtered-plan absence assertions with no\n positive control) · e39f (an inbound link removal NEVER CONVERGES when a pair holds two relations — I\n settled the question 2b16's agent could not: `add_dependency` is idempotent on `(target_id, relation)`\n while unlink resolves on TARGET ONLY, so two relations CAN coexist and G5 declines forever with no\n alert) · 6c0a (extract the issuelinks enrichment merge; 2b16's G1 evidence rests on\n `_enrich_like_fetcher`, a hand copy of `fetcher.py:592-596` that will silently drift and disarm the one\n guard between a truncated read and deleted local data).\n\n--- NEXT ACTIONS, in order ---\n 1. Land 1276 (2b16) once LLM-Review +1 AND Verified +1. Then close 2b16 (`--class preexisting`).\n 2. THEN implement 88d9 — plan certified, ticket claimed, seam pre-chosen. Respect the 3-line headroom.\n 3. Land the 5200 test repairs.\n 4. Dispatch the harness: `gh workflow run external-integration.yml --ref main` (job `jira-dc-harness`).\n    Read the per-cell verdicts AND the `[jira-live-canary] collected=N executed=N skipped=0` line.\n 5. Tick 5200's 18 ACs — criterion 11 needs the row-1 cell landed, and its row-12/row-14 deviations\n    recorded (the AC-verification comment on 5200 has the detail and the reasoning).\n 6. Close 5200, then e369 — **e369's own plan review is stale-code and must be re-run before its close.**"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785728846824018001,"uuid":"aaf8c926-305e-4140-930f-c8e75b447b84"}